%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAh...\d%K%P
「啊…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHello. The moon is... beautiful tonight, isn't it?\d%K%P
「辛苦了。\n今天…新月真是漂亮呢」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...You sure can tell that from inside the house, huh.\d%K%P
「…还真亏你能明白」%K%P
I found her right away. There was no need to even look for\nher.%K%P
立即就找到了美都子。\n就连特地去找的必要也没有。%K%P
As I knew the place she would always be at when she had\nsomething on her mind.%K%P
因为我知道，这孩子在想要一个人独处时，\n必定会来到一个相同的地方。%K%P
And I somehow knew that today was that kind of day.%K%P
然后今天也是，\n肯定会想要一个人呆着，这样的想法很轻易就被我察觉到了。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAt any rate... What a crazy day. So many things happened\ntoday.\d%K%P
「不过话说回来啊…\n今天实在是发生了很多事」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYeah.\d%K%P
「的确是」%K%P
I became formally employed. And even Ms. Kaya had found a\nnew job.%K%P
继我的正式聘用决定后，\n夏夜小姐的再就职也被发现了。%K%P
It was a joyous occasion. After all, the employment rate\nof the Terrace House Hinosaka's occupants had suddenly\njumped to a total of forty percent.%K%P
这是Terrace House阳之坂的成年人的就业率，\n一口气上升了４成的，值得纪念的日子。%K%P
...Which amounted to an increase of exactly forty percent\nfrom before.%K%P
…虽然上升了４成，不过总共也只有４成吧。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThings are finally moving along now... I'd have liked if\nthings had gone this way right from spring, though.\d%K%P
「这么多好的预兆，真不错呢。\n…如果能从春天开始的话就更好了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dY-Yeah...\d%K%P
「嗯、嗯…」%K%P
We'd definitely started from rock bottom at that time...\nand in Mitoko's case, doubly so.%K%P
春天那时的确是最差的开始了。\n比起我来，美都子那边更甚。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWell, no point complaining about it now or else it's\ngonna let our happiness slip away.\d%K%P
「嘛，但发牢骚还是免了。\n幸福会逃走的～」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI thought people said that about sighs.\d%K%P
「应该是悲叹吧」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAre the two even different?\d%K%P
「不是差不多的嘛」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI guess they aren't.\d%K%P
「那倒是」%K%P
After all, my happiness kept slipping away regardless of\nwhether or not I sighed, complained, or tried to act as\npositive as possible.%K%P
因为至今为止，吐露怨言也好，发出悲叹也好，\n甚至是虚张声势地努力也好，\n都让幸福毫不客气地逃跑了。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dYou'll be getting busy starting tomorrow, Osamu. You'll\nhave to pay back for April in September.\d%K%P
「从明天开始就要忙起来了哦，理君。\n４月欠下的债必须在９月还上哦」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'll do everything in my power to make that happen.\d%K%P
「我会向着那个方向努力的…」%K%P
I'd kinda been doing that from the start, though... I\nthink.%K%P
虽然我觉得至今为止都不是没有努力吧…%K%P
But this time, I wouldn't just put in the effort. I'd be\nsure to actually reap the fruits of my effort.%K%P
所以这次的『努力』，\n姑且以『回报』来作为重点吧。%K%P
...At the very least, until I got my first paycheck.%K%P
…至少在拿到第一份工资前是这样啦。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, but still... depending on how much work this job's\ngoing to be, I might not be able to help you study as\noften.\d%K%P
「啊，还有啊…\n抱歉，以后也许家教的时间要不规则了」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAh... True.\d%K%P
「啊～…是啊」%K%P
After all, when I was employed by that company last time,\nI would only find my way back home after midnight.%K%P
就算是在以前那样工作的时候，\n也只是每天在上午进行的教学。%K%P
The prospects of getting home in time to tutor her between\n8 and 10 were looking pretty grim indeed.%K%P
从晚上８点到１０点进行的家庭教师工作，\n照现在的情况看来，有很大的几率几乎是绝望的…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm sorry. I know we just started and everything. But\nI'll do all I can to at least be able to teach you on\nSundays...!\d%K%P
「抱歉，明明只是刚刚开始的。\n但是，至少在周日让我继续…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dIt's fine. Really, don't worry about it...\d%K%P
「不用了，\n不用啦…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dBut...\d%K%P
「可是…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAs long as you're working hard for your own sake, that's\nfine by me.\d%K%P
「理君只要努力做自己的事就好了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dMitoko...\d%K%P
「美都子…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThat'd give me motivation too, after all. As long as I\nknow you're happy, I can just relax and focus on taking\ncare of myself.\d%K%P
「这样的话我也会努力的。\n理君能幸福的话，我也就能放心努力做好自己的事了」%K%P
I could tell those were Mitoko's genuine feelings, without\nany hint of anxiety or resignation that would dilute her\nsincerity.%K%P
那份话语，认真且不包含任何嘲笑、不耐烦和放弃的意思，\n只是将美都子原本最真实的想法直接传达给了我。%K%P
I wasn't sure if, as her guardian, I should be happy that\nshe felt that way, but...%K%P
这些，都让我这个监护人感到羞愧啊。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThanks.\d%K%P
「谢谢」%K%P
As her kind and caring words seeped into my heart, in that\nmoment, I could feel my resolve growing strong once more.%K%P
那时的我，只是把那份话语铭记在心中，\n并且再次奠定了为这孩子而努力的决心。%K%P
